  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CHEMICALCOORDINATIONANDINTEGRATION_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Anatomy of thyroid and parathyroid glands</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The schematic diagram below represents the dorsal view of a gland located on either side of the trachea. Identify the thin flap of connective tissue labeled <strong>Q</strong> and the four small glands labeled <strong>R</strong>.</p>
      <p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 250" width="360" height="250">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="360" height="250" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <!-- Trachea -->
          <rect x="150" y="30" width="60" height="190" rx="8" fill="#e6e9ed" stroke="#4a5568" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="150" y1="165" x2="210" y2="165" stroke="#718096" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="150" y1="185" x2="210" y2="185" stroke="#718096" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="150" y1="205" x2="210" y2="205" stroke="#718096" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Thyroid lobes -->
          <ellipse cx="122" cy="110" rx="34" ry="52" fill="#f6c1c7" stroke="#9b2c2c" stroke-width="2"/>
          <ellipse cx="238" cy="110" rx="34" ry="52" fill="#f6c1c7" stroke="#9b2c2c" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Isthmus -->
          <rect x="148" y="98" width="64" height="24" rx="4" fill="#f6c1c7" stroke="#9b2c2c" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Four parathyroid glands on dorsal side -->
          <circle cx="122" cy="82" r="8" fill="#c53030" stroke="#742a2a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="122" cy="138" r="8" fill="#c53030" stroke="#742a2a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="238" cy="82" r="8" fill="#c53030" stroke="#742a2a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="238" cy="138" r="8" fill="#c53030" stroke="#742a2a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Labels and leader lines -->
          <line x1="100" y1="58" x2="55" y2="45" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="36" y="49" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">P</text>
          <line x1="180" y1="110" x2="180" y2="42" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="174" y="34" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">Q</text>
          <line x1="246" y1="82" x2="305" y2="65" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="246" y1="138" x2="305" y2="65" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="312" y="70" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">R</text>
          <line x1="210" y1="195" x2="295" y2="195" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="302" y="200" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">S</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Layout and Given Conditions</strong><br/>The schematic shows a bilobed endocrine gland positioned on either side of the trachea (<strong>S</strong>). The two lobes (<strong>P</strong>) are joined across the midline by a narrow connecting band (<strong>Q</strong>), and four small rounded glands (<strong>R</strong>) are embedded on the dorsal surface, one pair on each lobe.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>In human anatomy, the thyroid gland consists of two lobes located on either side of the trachea and interconnected by a thin flap of connective tissue. Four parathyroid glands are situated on the back (dorsal) side of the thyroid gland.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Identification of Structures</strong><br/>The connecting flap of connective tissue labeled <strong>Q</strong> is the isthmus, and the four small dorsal glands labeled <strong>R</strong> (one pair in each lobe of the thyroid) are the parathyroid glands.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Final Answer</strong><br/><strong>Q</strong> represents the isthmus and <strong>R</strong> represents the parathyroid glands.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Q:</strong> Isthmus; <strong>R:</strong> Parathyroid glands</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Q:</strong> Infundibulum; <strong>R:</strong> Thymus lobes</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Q:</strong> Sella tursica; <strong>R:</strong> Pineal glands</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Q:</strong> Corpus luteum; <strong>R:</strong> Adrenal glands</p>]]></text></answer>
