  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CHEMICALCOORDINATIONANDINTEGRATION_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Adrenal gland section and associated hormones</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The diagram shows a gland situated at the anterior part of the kidney along with its cross-section divided into an outer region <strong>M</strong> and a central region <strong>N</strong>. Identify the hormones secreted by <strong>N</strong> and the disorder caused by underproduction of hormones from <strong>M</strong>.</p>
      <p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 240" width="380" height="240">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="380" height="240" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <!-- Kidney + Adrenal gland (a) -->
          <ellipse cx="95" cy="145" rx="42" ry="62" fill="#d69e2e" stroke="#744210" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M 65 92 Q 95 45 125 92 Q 95 102 65 92 Z" fill="#f6e05e" stroke="#975a16" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="72" y="150" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">Kidney</text>
          <!-- Arrow to section -->
          <path d="M 128 72 Q 165 55 190 70" fill="none" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="195,73 185,65 187,76" fill="#1a202c"/>
          <!-- Enlarged section (b) -->
          <path d="M 205 180 L 265 45 L 345 180 Z" fill="#f6e05e" stroke="#975a16" stroke-width="2.5"/>
          <path d="M 225 168 L 265 78 L 325 168 Z" fill="#fc8181" stroke="#9b2c2c" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Labels -->
          <line x1="252" y1="62" x2="215" y2="35" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="198" y="34" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">M</text>
          <line x1="272" y1="132" x2="340" y2="115" stroke="#1a202c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="346" y="120" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#1a202c">N</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Layout and Given Conditions</strong><br/>The left part of the diagram shows an adrenal gland positioned at the anterior end of a kidney. The enlarged cross-section on the right distinguishes an outer peripheral region (<strong>M</strong>) and a centrally located core tissue (<strong>N</strong>).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>Each adrenal gland is composed of two distinct tissues: the outer adrenal cortex (<strong>M</strong>) and the centrally located adrenal medulla (<strong>N</strong>).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Functional Analysis</strong><br/>The central adrenal medulla (<strong>N</strong>) secretes two catecholamine hormones: adrenaline (epinephrine) and noradrenaline (norepinephrine). The outer adrenal cortex (<strong>M</strong>) secretes corticoids (glucocorticoids, mineralocorticoids, and small amounts of androgenic steroids). Underproduction of hormones by the adrenal cortex alters carbohydrate metabolism, causing acute weakness and fatigue, which leads to Addison's disease.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Final Answer</strong><br/>Region <strong>N</strong> secretes adrenaline and noradrenaline, and underproduction of hormones from region <strong>M</strong> causes Addison's disease.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>N</strong> secretes cortisol and aldosterone; underproduction from <strong>M</strong> causes Graves' disease.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>N</strong> secretes adrenaline and noradrenaline; underproduction from <strong>M</strong> causes Addison's disease.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>N</strong> secretes glucagon and insulin; underproduction from <strong>M</strong> causes Diabetes Insipidus.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>N</strong> secretes thymosins; underproduction from <strong>M</strong> causes cretinism.</p>]]></text></answer>
